cff-version: "1.2.0"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "ConnectomeKG: Connectomes as Knowledge Graphs"
abstract: >
  ConnectomeKG turns an electron-microscopy connectome into a queryable
  knowledge graph. Neurons, cell types, neuropils, hemilineages, taxa and
  community labels are nodes; synapse edges carry counts and transmitter
  signs. It supports semantic search over the cell type and neuropil
  vocabulary, strongest signed paths, upstream and downstream cones, and a
  Markdown analysis. The first corpus is the FlyWire FAFB v783 adult
  Drosophila brain.
